# Per-machine configuration for data-orchestrator.
#
# Copy this file to ".env" and set the data-source roots for THIS machine.
# ".env" is git-ignored, so each machine can keep its own paths.
#
#   cp .env.example .env      # macOS / Linux
#   Copy-Item .env.example .env   # PowerShell
#
# Each data source has its own *_ROOT key pointing at the folder that contains
# the source's "raw/" directory. A CLI flag (e.g. --root) always overrides these.
#
# Values are taken literally: no $VAR expansion, surrounding quotes stripped.
# No inline comments: a "#" after a value is part of the value.
# A key already set in the real environment always wins over this file.
#
# Which file is read: DATA_ORCHESTRATOR_DOTENV if set in the real environment
# (never from a .env; a missing file is an error, exit 2), else the nearest
# .env in the current directory or its parents, else the one at this repo's
# root. Every run prints "Config: .env = <path>" (or "no .env file found").
# DATA_ORCHESTRATOR_DOTENV=/path/to/this-machine.env

# --- cb_corpus ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Folder that contains "raw/<bank>/<doctype>/<year>/<doc_id>.<ext>".
CB_CORPUS_ROOT=/path/to/data/cb_corpus

# --- company_corpus -----------------------------------------------------------
# SEC EDGAR micro layer. Folder that holds the company_corpus data dir (the one
# its renderer writes the page-anchored PDFs / cleaned text into). Optional: if
# unset, company_corpus falls back to its own default data dir. A CLI --root
# always overrides this.
COMPANY_CORPUS_ROOT=/path/to/data/company_corpus

# --- future sources ----------------------------------------------------------
# Add one *_ROOT per new source connector as they are added, e.g.:
# REPEC_ROOT=

# --- Vault and Qdrant ----------------------------------------------------------
# Vault Postgres (rag_ingestions state + vault-source selection)
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:pass@host:5432/documents
# Qdrant the engine writes to (the NAS one since 2026-11). The engine defaults
# to localhost:6333, the LEGACY store: always set host and port explicitly.
QDRANT_HOST=localhost
QDRANT_PORT=6433
# API key of that Qdrant (blank or unset = none). Never commit the real one.
QDRANT_API_KEY=
# true only if Qdrant is served over TLS (default false: plain HTTP; with a key
# qdrant-client then warns "Api key is used with an insecure connection").
# QDRANT_HTTPS=false
# Seconds a request to Qdrant may take (default 60).
# RAG_ENGINE_QDRANT_TIMEOUT=60

# --- Ingestion engine (rag-engine) ---------------------------------------------
# The engine is a dependency of this package (no separate checkout, no path
# key). It reads the variables below from the process environment: they must
# be in this file (or the real environment), there is no other .env.
#
# OCR of scanned pages. With "--ocr auto" (the default) OCR runs only when BOTH
# are set: ENABLE_OCR=true and TESSDATA_PREFIX (the folder holding Tesseract's
# *.traineddata files, or its parent). Left out, "auto" silently means "never";
# every run prints "OCR: available (...)" or "OCR: off (...)".
# ENABLE_OCR=true
# TESSDATA_PREFIX=/usr/share/tesseract-ocr/5/tessdata
# Tesseract languages used by OCR, joined by "+" (default eng). The engine uses
# exactly this list, whatever language files are installed.
# RAG_ENGINE_OCR_LANGUAGES=eng
# Points per write to Qdrant (default 100).
# RAG_ENGINE_BATCH_SIZE=100
# Leave RAG_ENGINE_BACKEND unset: ingestion uses the torch backend installed
# with this package.

# --- data-orchestrator options -----------------------------------------------
# All optional; leave commented out to keep the built-in defaults.
# Embedding model behind the routed collection name (default
# intfloat/multilingual-e5-base; CI swaps in a tiny model for integration runs).
# DATA_ORCHESTRATOR_EMBEDDING_MODEL=
# Vector dimension of that model: required for any model but the default
# (768); a value that is not the loaded model's is a fatal error.
# DATA_ORCHESTRATOR_EMBEDDING_DIM=
# (RAG_ENGINE_MODEL / RAG_ENGINE_DIM, the engine's own names for these two,
# are read when the keys above are unset.)
# Level of the log lines sent to stderr (the engine's included): DEBUG, INFO
# (default), WARNING, ERROR, CRITICAL.
# DATA_ORCHESTRATOR_LOG_LEVEL=INFO
# Directory for the --no-vault JSON-lines ledger and run reports (default
# <repo>/state).
# DATA_ORCHESTRATOR_STATE_DIR=
# Comma list narrowing the MIME types the vault selection offers to the engine
# (default: every type the pinned rag-engine reads; an unknown type -> exit 2).
# DATA_ORCHESTRATOR_SUPPORTED_MIME_TYPES=
# Failed/attempted ratio above which a run is "degraded" (exit 3); plain decimal
# in [0, 1], default 0.10. 0 = any failure degrades, 1 = ratio rule off.
# DATA_ORCHESTRATOR_DEGRADED_FAILURE_RATIO=
